  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Until now you've used は to mark the topic: 私は がくせいです (As for me, I'm a student). When you want to say 'X too' or 'X also', you swap は out for も. The rest of the sentence stays exactly the same, word for word: topic, then the particle, then the noun, then です. So 私は やすみです (I'm off) becomes 私も やすみです (I'm off too). も does the 'too' job and the topic job together, so you never write は and も side by side.",
    "structure_notes": [
      "Slot order doesn't change: [Topic] + も + [Noun] + です. Only the particle after the topic changes, from は to も.",
      "も goes right after the thing that is 'also' true. In 私の よていも えいがです, the 'also' belongs to 私の よてい (my plan), so も comes after that whole phrase.",
      "Never use は and も together. も replaces は completely. 私はも is wrong.",
      "To ask a question, add か at the end the usual way: ゆきも やすみですか。= Are you off too, Yuki?",
      "In English, 'too' comes at the end of the sentence, but in Japanese も comes right after the word it's about, near the start of the sentence."
    ],
    "connects_to": "This is the same 〜は〜です frame from episode 1, with も in the topic marker's place. It also works with の phrases from earlier episodes: 私の よていも… attaches も to the whole 'my plan' chunk, just as は would."
  },
